TerraGear dependency and build notes
====================================

TerraGear requires CMake 3.20 or newer and a C++17 compiler. The current
supported dependency baseline is:

  * CGAL 6.x
  * SimGear 2024.1 or newer
  * Boost (system and thread components)
  * GDAL 2.0 or newer
  * ZLIB, TIFF, and Threads

Build and install SimGear before configuring TerraGear. SimGear must be
installed with its CMake package files. If it is installed outside the
standard prefix, set CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH to its install prefix or provide
SimGear_DIR pointing to the directory containing SimGearConfig.cmake.

Configure and build TerraGear from the stable source directory:

  cmake -S . -B build
  cmake --build build --parallel
  ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

If CGAL is installed in a non-standard prefix, set CGAL_DIR to the directory
containing CGALConfig.cmake when configuring. The build uses the exported
CGAL::CGAL and SimGearCore targets so their include paths and transitive
dependencies are supplied by the dependency packages. The CGAL compatibility
test checks polygon triangulation with and without a hole, KD-tree spatial
queries, and segment intersections.
